 ### [Maximum Intensity Projection (MIP)](10702-maximum-intensity-projection-mip.md)
-Maximum Intensity Projection (MIP) projects the maximum scalar value encountered along each viewing ray onto the 2D image plane. It is primarily used to highlight high-intensity structures, such as blood vessels in angiography or bone in CT scans, by suppressing lower-intensity background noise. Unlike standard front-to-back compositing which blends all samples, MIP discards all intermediate values in favor of the single maximum, which causes it to lose depth differentiation and the ability to distinguish whether the maximum lies in the front or back of the volume.
